Task Tracker (MERN)
A full‑stack task management app built with the MERN stack. Users can register and log in, then create, update, delete, filter, and toggle tasks with priorities and due dates. The project is deployed with a Node/Express backend and MongoDB Atlas, and a React frontend hosted separately.

Features
User authentication with JWT (register and login)

Password hashing using bcrypt

Task CRUD: create, read, update, delete

Mark tasks as pending / completed (status toggle)

Priority levels: low, medium, high

Optional due date for each task

Filters: All / Pending / Completed

Task stats: total, completed, pending

Responsive, modern UI built with React and custom CSS

Deployed backend (Render) + frontend (Vercel) using MongoDB Atlas for persistence

Tech Stack
Frontend

React (Create React App)

Axios for API calls

React Router for routing

Context API for auth state management

Backend

Node.js + Express

MongoDB + Mongoose

JWT (jsonwebtoken)

bcrypt for password hashing

dotenv for environment variables

CORS middleware

Infrastructure

MongoDB Atlas (cloud database)

Render (Node/Express API hosting)

Vercel (React app hosting)

Project Structure
text
task-tracker-mern/
  client/           # React frontend
    src/
      api/         # Axios instance + auth/task API helpers
      pages/       # Login, Dashboard
      context/     # AuthContext (user + token)
      index.css    # Global styling
  server/           # Node/Express backend
    models/        # User, Task schemas
    controllers/   # authController, taskController
    routes/        # authRoutes, taskRoutes
    middleware/    # authMiddleware (JWT)
    utils/         # token helper (signToken)
    index.js       # Express app + Mongo connection
Getting Started (Local Development)
1. Prerequisites
Node.js (LTS) installed

MongoDB running locally or a MongoDB Atlas connection string

2. Clone and install
bash
git clone https://github.com/<your-username>/task-tracker-mern.git
cd task-tracker-mern
Backend

bash
cd server
npm install
Create server/.env:

text
PORT=5000
MONGO_URI=mongodb://127.0.0.1:27017/tasktracker   # or your Atlas URI
JWT_SECRET=supersecretkey123
JWT_EXPIRES_IN=7d
Run backend:

bash
npm run dev
Frontend

bash
cd ../client
npm install
In client/package.json, keep:

json
"proxy": "http://localhost:5000"
Run frontend:

bash
npm start
App will be available at http://localhost:3000, talking to the backend at http://localhost:5000 via the proxy.

API Overview
Auth
POST /api/auth/register

Body: { "email": string, "password": string }

Response: { token, user: { id, email } }

POST /api/auth/login

Body: { "email": string, "password": string }

Response: { token, user: { id, email } }

Tasks (protected – requires Authorization: Bearer <token>)
GET /api/tasks?status=pending|completed

POST /api/tasks

{ title, priority, dueDate }

PUT /api/tasks/:id

PATCH /api/tasks/:id/toggle (flip pending/completed)

DELETE /api/tasks/:id

Deployment
Backend
Hosted on Render as a Node/Express web service with root directory server.

Build command: npm install

Start command: npm start

Environment variables set in Render dashboard: MONGO_URI, JWT_SECRET, JWT_EXPIRES_IN, PORT (optional).

Frontend
Hosted on Vercel with root directory client.

Build command: npm run build, output build.

client/src/api/http.js uses:

js
baseURL =
  process.env.NODE_ENV === "production"
    ? "https://<your-render-service>.onrender.com/api"
    : "/api";
So local dev calls the proxy, and production calls the Render API directly.
